<p id="p2">I’m pleased to announce my latest free and open-source project, which I’ve been working on for the past six months: <a href="https://github.com/viticci/MacRemote" rel="noopener noreferrer">MacRemote</a>, a Mac app that lets you securely connect your Mac’s tools and local MCPs to any AI agent of your choice.</p>
<p id="p3">You can find the notarized app, extensive <a href="https://github.com/viticci/MacRemote/blob/main/README.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">documentation</a> for people and agents, and <a href="https://github.com/viticci/MacRemote" rel="noopener noreferrer">the source code on GitHub</a>.</p>
<p id="p4">I released MacRemote as a private beta for Club MacStories members <a href="https://www.macstories.net/club/macstories-weekly-issue-537/introducing-macremote-bridge-your-local-macs-tools-and-mcps-to-any-ai-agent/" rel="noopener noreferrer">two weeks ago</a>, and after lots of feedback and some feature additions, I think it is ready for its public debut. I’ve been using MacRemote with all my agents on any device and cloud environment since May and, honestly, I can’t imagine living without it.</p>
<p id="p5"><!--more--></p>
<p id="p6">Here’s the gist of MacRemote: it’s a Mac app, which contains an MCP server that exposes user-selected tools (CLIs) and MCP servers from <em>your</em> Mac to any MCP-compatible AI app that wants to connect to it. MacRemote effectively serves as a bridge between your Mac and any other agent by opening a secure, permission-based <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/tunnel/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare tunnel</a> that can either live at a randomized domain or be hosted under a domain you own. You’re <strong>always in control</strong>: you can choose the authentication system you prefer, grant granular permissions on a per-app basis, revoke and grant specific tools at any time, and, of course, accept or deny agents that want to connect to it.</p>
<p id="p7">MacRemote is compliant with the <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28" rel="noopener noreferrer">most recent MCP spec</a> and supports modern features of MCP such as long-running <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/tasks/overview" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tasks</a>, file <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/community/working-groups/file-uploads" rel="noopener noreferrer">uploads</a>, <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/skills/overview" rel="noopener noreferrer">skills</a> over MCP, <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/apps/overview" rel="noopener noreferrer">MCP Apps</a>, and more. It is also backwards-compatible with clients that use an older MCP spec.</p>
