<p id="p18">I’ve spent a lot of time testing and thinking about the architecture of MacRemote, as well as keeping up with the latest additions to the MCP spec. Today, MacRemote already supports passing <a href="https://claude.com/resources/articles/skills-over-mcp-tasks-and-more" rel="noopener noreferrer">skills over MCP to Claude</a> and other clients that use the latest version of the protocol; it also comes with built-in support for my CLIs (<a href="https://github.com/viticci/frames-cli" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple Frames</a> and <a href="https://github.com/viticci/remctl" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reminders</a>), which will soon be joined by Apple Notes, Mail, Photos, and Apple Music once they’ve been tested by Club MacStories members.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/11/26/shortcut-upload-1795709815235-e73ceb57fa.png" alt="An example of a long-running task being executed on my Mac, via MacRemote’s MCP Tasks, from the app I’m working on."><p class="image-caption">An example of a long-running task being executed on my Mac, via MacRemote’s MCP Tasks, from the app I’m working on.</p></div>
